.TH tucodepng n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tucodepng
.PP
Render a character\-code table (a classic code\-page grid) to a PNG. Data comes from \fBtclutils::tucode\fR (\fBlookup\fR); drawing from \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR. Pure Tcl.
.CS
package require tclutils::tucodepng
tclutils::tucodepng::write ascii.png 0 127 -title "ASCII 0-127" -shownames 1
set png [tclutils::tucodepng::latin1 -shownames 1]   ;# 128..255 -> PNG bytes
.CE
.SS API
.IP \(bu
\fBrender from to ?opts?\fR \-> PNG bytes (range within 0..255).
.IP \(bu
\fBwrite file from to ?opts?\fR \-> writes the PNG, returns the filename.
.IP \(bu
\fBascii ?opts?\fR (0..127), \fBlatin1 ?opts?\fR (128..255), \fBall ?opts?\fR (0..255).
.PP
Each cell shows the hex code (top), the glyph (centre) and, with \fB\-shownames\fR, the name (bottom). Control codes (0..31, 127) show their abbreviation (NUL, ESC, ...); 32 shows "SP".
.SS Options
.PP
\fB\-columns N\fR (default 16), \fB\-scale N\fR (default 2), \fB\-theme default|dark|light\fR, \fB\-showcode 0|1\fR (default 1), \fB\-shownames 0|1\fR (default 0), \fB\-title TEXT\fR, \fB\-textcmd CMD\fR.
.SS "Real glyphs for Latin\-1 (\-textcmd)"
.PP
The built\-in 6x8 bitmap font covers ASCII (and German umlauts), so 0..127 renders fully dependency\-free. For the real Latin\-1 glyphs (128..255) pass a \fB\-textcmd\fR that fills outline glyphs from a real font (Glyphs + tupngdraw \fBfillcontours\fR); hex codes, names and control abbreviations always use the bitmap font. The command is called \fB{*}$CMD img x y w h char color\fR per printable cell \-\- same hook as tumonthpng. See examples/generate\-codepage\-glyphs\-demo.tcl.
